      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～を{誇|ほこ}る: to be proud of ~, to boast ~\n- ～に{誇|ほこ}れる: to be able to be proud of (toward ~)\n- {世界|せかい}に{誇|ほこ}る: to be proud of on a world stage\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {歴史|れきし}を{誇|ほこ}る: to boast a history\n- {伝統|でんとう}を{誇|ほこ}る: to take pride in tradition\n- {実績|じっせき}を{誇|ほこ}る: to boast achievements\n- {誇|ほこ}りに{思|おも}う: to feel proud (related noun form)\n\nUSAGE:\nWhen the subject is a place, company, or country, sense 1 (legitimate pride) is typical. When the subject is a person showing off, it can shade into sense 2 (boasting). The potential form {誇|ほこ}れる is common in positive contexts: {世界|せかい}に{誇|ほこ}れる (something to be proud of internationally).",
